TEXT_SETTINGS_CONTEXT_MENU_TITLE        = Context menu
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_NOTE                  = Menu entries are static registry verbs and need no administrator rights; on Windows 11 they live under "Show more options".
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_AUTO_EXTRACT_HINT     = Auto extract looks at what the archive holds: a lone file comes out as-is; everything under one top-level folder releases that whole folder without wrapping it in a second copy of itself; anything else goes into a new folder named after the archive, using "name (2)", "name (3)" when that name is taken.
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_COMPRESS_FILES        = Add "Compress as" entries for all files
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_COMPRESS_FOLDERS      = Add "Compress as" entries for folders
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_EXTRACT               = Add "Extract" entries for associated archives
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_EXTRACT_HINT          = This one follows the file associations: with nothing associated yet it has nothing to act on. Double-click behaviour is not decided here — see "General → On double-clicking an archive".
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_UNSUPPORTED           = The context menu can only be configured on Windows.
TEXT_SETTINGS_CTX_FAILED                = Writing the context menu entries failed:
TEXT_BTN_SET_DEFAULT                    = Set as default...
TEXT_SETTINGS_DEFAULT_STILL             = These formats are associated, but another program is still the default (Windows default-app protection). Click "Set as default..." and pick Andzip in the system settings: ${list}

; ---- Settings: compression page ----
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_TITLE            = Compression settings
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_DEFAULT_LEVEL    = Default compression level
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_LEVEL_HINT       = Which entry the dropdown opens on in "New archive". The first three are about speed, Normal balances speed against ratio, Maximum only cares about ratio.
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_NO_ROOT          = Do not create a root folder when compressing a single folder
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_NO_ROOT_HINT     = When on, the archive holds the folder's contents directly instead of the folder itself.
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_EXCLUDE_THUMBS   = Exclude Thumbs.db
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_EXCLUDE_TYPES    = File types to exclude when compressing
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_EXCLUDE_HINT     = Semicolon-separated name patterns, e.g. *.bak; *.tmp;. Empty means nothing extra is excluded. Patterns match the file name, not its directory.
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_TEST_AFTER       = Test the archive after compression
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_KEEP_PROGRESS    = Keep the progress window open when compression finishes
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_KEEP_PROGRESS_HINT = When off the progress bar disappears as soon as it completes; when on it stays with the result. Useful for checking the ratio.
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_OUTPUT_DIR       = Output folder
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_OUTPUT_LAST      = The folder used for the last new archive
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_OUTPUT_FIXED     = Always output to this folder
TEXT_SETTINGS_COMPRESS_OUTPUT_FIXED_HINT = Leaving it empty behaves like "the folder used for the last new archive".

; ---- Settings: extraction page ----
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_TITLE             = Extraction settings
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_SINGLE_FILE_TO_FOLDER = Auto extract: put a lone file into a new folder too
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_SINGLE_FILE_HINT  = Off by default: an archive holding one file simply releases that file. When on, a folder named after that file is created (photo.jpg.gz becomes photo\photo.jpg), using "name (2)", "name (3)" when the name is taken.
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_OPEN_FOLDER       = Open the folder after extraction
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_OPEN_FOLDER_HINT  = Only opens once extraction actually finished; a failure or a cancel never pops open a half-filled directory.
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_KEEP_PROGRESS     = Keep the progress window open when extraction finishes
TEXT_SETTINGS_EXTRACT_KEEP_PROGRESS_HINT = Applies to "Extract files" in the main window only. The right-click and double-click paths still disappear when done, deliberately, and do not follow this setting.

